# A read of an array element that a test has found present is a load and nothing else. It compares with no length, looks for no hole and has no arm for a position that is no index, so a function that only tests and reads calls nothing and has no frame.
# Its result is an element: the type has no `undefined`, and a number comes out unboxed. It asks nothing of the prototypes, so none of these arrays is pristine.
# Inside the length of storage of doubles the same holds for a read that takes a hole for NaN. Beside each stands the read that may find nothing
# FORM: Placed
# OPTIONS: heat=OnlyLoopsAreHot check=validate-back-end
# RUN: generate-code calls
# RUN(S): code-shapes
# RUN(R): pass ChooseRepresentations

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="presentInInt32AtIndex" parameters=[{type=Array<i32, proven, Int32>}, {type=int[0, 4294967294]}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v2 = IsElementPresent v0, v1 arrayStorage=Int32
    TestAndBranch v2 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2()
  b1(v3):
    v4 = GetArrayElement v0, v1, v3 arrayStorage=Int32 level=Proven [isPresent]
    Return v4
  b2():
    v5 = Undefined
    Return v5
}
